      "writtenOn": "2023-05-18T07:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this method clear the list of tethered clients, or the list of local-only clients, depending on whether the IpServer that became inactive was tethering or local-only?\n\nAs far as I can tell, this updateConnectedClients will call ConnectedClientsTracker#updateConnectedClients. That code *tries* to remove the clients from IpServers that don\u0027t have IP addresses, but then it does this:\n\n        // Add connected WiFi clients that do not have any known address\n        for (MacAddress client : wifiClientMacs) {\n            if (clientsMap.containsKey(client)) continue;\n            clientsMap.put(client, new TetheredClient(\n                    client, Collections.emptyList() /* addresses */, TETHERING_WIFI));\n        }\n\nwhich will put the clients back.\n\nIf the above is correct, then I think there\u0027s a bug in this code that when an IpServer goes down, all the clients that it had are still in the list, but without IP addresses.\n\nAm I reading this correctly? Do we have a test for this already? If not, can you add one?",
